UID:20260910-Free2Klaunches2000seats@nyc-calendar
DTSTAMP:20260827T132941Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260910
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260911
SUMMARY:Free 2-K launches: 2\,000 seats
DESCRIPTION:The first free 2-K seats open in four communities\, announced
  with Gov. Kathy Hochul in March\, expanding to universality within four
  years. Reporting puts services beginning in September\; no exact launch
  date has been announced\, so this is pegged to the start of the school 
 year.\n\nhttps://www.nyc.gov/mayors-office/news/2026/03/mayor-mamdani-an
 d-governor-hochul-announce-first-four-communitie
URL:https://www.nyc.gov/mayors-office/news/2026/03/mayor-mamdani-and-gove
 rnor-hochul-announce-first-four-communitie
CATEGORIES:cityhall
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20260910-Firstdayofschool@nyc-calendar
DTSTAMP:20260827T132941Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260910
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260911
SUMMARY:First day of school
DESCRIPTION:New York City Public Schools: "The new school year starts on 
 Thursday\, September 10\, 2026." An unusually late start — Labor Day fal
 ls on Sept. 7 — and the year runs to June 28\, 2027 to reach the 180 ins
 tructional days the state requires. Some 800\,000 children return to K-1
 2 classrooms\, a number that has fallen roughly 10% since 2020. Students
 ' first day off is Sept. 21 for Yom Kippur.\n\nhttps://www.schools.nyc.g
 ov/calendar/2026-2027-school-year-calendar
URL:https://www.schools.nyc.gov/calendar/2026-2027-school-year-calendar
CATEGORIES:city-life
END:VEVENT
